 projects/lumen/package-lock.json              |  3 +-
 projects/lumen/package.json                   |  1 +
 .../lumen/scripts/predeploy-chunk-chain.ts    | 35 ++++++++++--
 projects/lumen/tests/metaverse.test.ts        |  3 +-
 .../lumen/tests/predeployReadonly.test.ts     | 55 +++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 100 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 projects/lumen/tests/predeployReadonly.test.ts

diff --git a/projects/lumen/docs/HOSTING_FLY.md b/projects/lumen/docs/HOSTING_FLY.md
index f67f881..992899a 100644
--- a/projects/lumen/docs/HOSTING_FLY.md
+++ b/projects/lumen/docs/HOSTING_FLY.md
@@ -121,6 +121,16 @@ fly secrets import -a lumen-tidepool < secrets.env
 
 ## Deploy one machine
 
+On a redeploy (a volume that already has data), check the chunk chain on a copy first. The check is read-only and never touches the live file. Skip it on the first deploy.
+
+```powershell
+fly ssh console -a lumen-tidepool -C "node -e \"new (require('node:sqlite').DatabaseSync)('/data/lumen.sqlite').exec(\\\"VACUUM INTO '/data/precheck.sqlite'\\\")\""
+fly ssh sftp get /data/precheck.sqlite ./precheck.sqlite -a lumen-tidepool
+$env:LUMEN_DATA = "./precheck.sqlite"; npm run predeploy
+```
+
+Exit code 1 means do not deploy: the desk would come up in degraded mode. Delete `precheck.sqlite` on both sides afterwards.
+
 ```powershell
 fly deploy --ha=false -a lumen-tidepool
 ```
